<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.73 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.73 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Cotton Export Corporation of Pakistan said on Friday cotton output in 1996/97 (July-June) had reached a provisional 8.73 million 375-lb bales by Thursday, compared to 9.93 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales (year-ago):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.647 (8.170)  2.084 (1.765)  8.731 (9.935)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.627 (8.168)  2.082 (1.760)  8.710 (9.929)</p>
<p> Mill sales     5.774 (6.856)  1.883 (1.262)  7.658 (8.118)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.008 (1.023)  0.006 (0.466)  0.014 (1.490)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   0.864 (0.290)  0.193 (0.035)  1.058 (0.326)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
